Step 1 – Initialize the AWS environment
No AWS resources will be created in this step
Objective: Establish the AWS account, account name and region as shell variables. All subsequent commands will reuse these variables.

For this training, we'll use:
Parameter	Value
Project name	student-ai-agent
AWS Region	ap-south-1
Account name	student-agent-training
AWS account ID	Retrieved automatically
Agent framework	Strands
Runtime	Amazon Bedrock AgentCore

=====
1.1 Create a project folder
Start a new Terminal session on your Mac.

Run:
mkdir -p ~/student-ai-agent-training
cd ~/student-ai-agent-training


This creates the project workspace.
1.2 Define the environment variables
Run:
export PROJECT_NAME="student-ai-agent"
export ACCOUNT_NAME="student-agent-training"

export AWS_REGION="ap-south-1"
export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION="$AWS_REGION"

export AWS_ACCOUNT_ID=$(aws sts get-caller-identity \
  --query Account \
  --output text)

export AWS_CALLER_ARN=$(aws sts get-caller-identity \
  --query Arn \
  --output text)

1.3 Verify the environment
Run:
echo "PROJECT       : $PROJECT_NAME"
echo "ACCOUNT NAME  : $ACCOUNT_NAME"
echo "ACCOUNT ID    : $AWS_ACCOUNT_ID"
echo "REGION        : $AWS_REGION"
echo "CALLER ARN    : $AWS_CALLER_ARN"

