Step 2 – Install and verify development tools
Objective: Prepare your MacBook to develop a Python-based Strands Agent and deploy it to Amazon Bedrock AgentCore.

We'll install and verify the tools before creating any AWS resources.

The development environment will use:
Tool	Purpose
AWS CLI	Communicate with AWS
Python 3.12 or later	Run the agent application
uv	Manage Python environments and packages
Node.js	Support development utilities where required
Git	Manage project source code
AgentCore starter toolkit	Develop and deploy agents to AgentCore

2.1 Check what is already installed
Run this block in your Terminal:

cat > setup-macos.sh <<'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

echo "======================================"
echo " Student AI Agent - macOS Setup"
echo "======================================"

# Install Homebrew if it is not already installed
if ! command -v brew >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "Installing Homebrew..."
    /bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"
