Step 3 – Create the Python project environment
Objective: Create an isolated Python 3.12 environment for our Strands Agent application.

We'll use uv to manage the Python environment and dependencies.

Run these commands from your project directory:
mkdir -p agent
cd agent

export PATH=$PATH:~/.local/bin
uv init --python 3.12

uv venv --python 3.12 .venv

source .venv/bin/activate


What are we doing?
Command	Purpose
mkdir -p agent	Creates the agent project directory
cd agent	Enters the directory
uv init --python 3.12	Initializes the Python project
uv venv --python 3.12 .venv	Creates an isolated environment
source .venv/bin/activate	Activates the environment

=============
Step 4 – Install Strands Agents and AWS SDK
Objective: Install the Python libraries required to build our Student AI Agent and communicate with AWS services.

We will install:
Package	Purpose
strands-agents	Framework for developing AI agents
boto3	Python SDK for invoking AWS services, including Lambda

4.1 Install the packages
Make sure you are inside the agent directory and the .venv environment is activated.

Run:
uv add strands-agents boto3


This command:
- Downloads the packages.
- Adds them as project dependencies in pyproject.toml.
- Creates or updates uv.lock.
- Installs them into the project's virtual environment.
4.2 Verify installation
Run:
python -c "from strands import Agent; import boto3; print('Strands Agents: OK'); print('Boto3: OK')"


