Step 7 – Configure Amazon Nova Lite
Objective: Configure our Strands Agent to use Amazon Nova Lite through Amazon Bedrock.
Parameter	Value
Agent framework	Strands
LLM provider	Amazon Bedrock
Foundation model	Amazon Nova Lite
Model ID	amazon.nova-lite-v1:0
Region	ap-south-1

7.1 Stop the local development server
If it is still running, press:
Ctrl + C

7.2 Set the model environment variables
Run:
export MODEL_PROVIDER="bedrock"
export MODEL_ID="amazon.nova-lite-v1:0"

export MODEL_INFERENCE_PROFILE_ARN="arn:aws:bedrock:${AWS_REGION}:${AWS_ACCOUNT_ID}:inference-profile/apac.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0"


7.3 Verify the configuration
echo "Model Provider: $MODEL_PROVIDER"
echo "Model ID: $MODEL_ID"
echo "Inference Profile: $MODEL_INFERENCE_PROFILE_ARN"

7.4 Important model access requirement
The AWS account must have access to Amazon Nova Lite in Amazon Bedrock, and the agent's IAM execution role must eventually have permission to invoke the inference profile.

We will configure the IAM permissions during the deployment preparation.

